 "honest": [
  "an era sign comparison is a statement about two LEVELS; the month-level rate beneath it is the one that says whether the tilt tracks the traded spread at all",
  "a month-level rate near 50% is a result, not a defect: it means the era agreement is carried by the level, and quoting the tilt as a timing signal is not supported",
  "the deadband is declared before the burn (10bp monthly): months where either series is inside it are excluded from the deadband rate, and the raw rate is printed beside it rather than replaced",
  "the engine series is the engine's own wide-vs-ladder monthly difference, so this compares a member ratio against a traded quantity, not two regressions",
  "eras remain calendar partitions of one continuous monthly series and do not add up",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no prereg, no trial count"
 ],
